{"id":"ux-visual-design","title":"UI/UX: visual design basics","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":173,"duration":172.66,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":474,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":12.325},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":12.325,"end":43.555},{"id":"explain2","title":"More basics","start":43.555,"end":76.545},{"id":"example","title":"Fix a screen","start":76.545,"end":106.155},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":106.155,"end":116.785},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":116.785,"end":125.905},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":125.905,"end":148.615},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":148.615,"end":172.66}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":3.29,"text":"Have you ever opened an app and missed the button you needed?","w":[0.56,0.74,0.9,1.16,1.44,1.66,2.1,2.26,2.48,2.6,2.86,2.98]},{"s":0,"a":3.74,"b":9.8,"text":"I'm Kora. Today we look at visual design basics for interfaces, so the screen shows you what matters first.","w":[3.88,4.06,4.88,5.2,5.34,5.54,5.66,6.06,6.44,6.82,6.98,7.84,7.98,8.1,8.52,8.76,8.88,9.04,9.38]},{"s":0,"a":10.1,"b":11.9,"text":"It is a simple skill you can learn.","w":[10.16,10.28,10.4,10.5,10.86,11.26,11.4,11.58]},{"s":1,"a":12.75,"b":16.11,"text":"Visual hierarchy means the most important thing is noticed first.","w":[12.8,13.24,13.84,14.1,14.26,14.56,14.98,15.18,15.34,15.7]},{"s":1,"a":16.41,"b":19.98,"text":"You create it with size, weight, colour and contrast, and position.","w":[16.44,16.64,17,17.1,17.32,17.88,18.3,18.68,18.82,19.42,19.54]},{"s":1,"a":20.28,"b":23.3,"text":"Bold text has more weight, so it pulls the eye.","w":[20.3,20.68,21.06,21.28,21.54,22.2,22.38,22.52,22.88,23.14]},{"s":1,"a":23.6,"b":27.76,"text":"People usually scan from the top, and in left to right languages from the left.","w":[23.62,23.98,24.36,24.7,24.86,24.98,25.78,25.92,26.04,26.28,26.4,26.58,27.1,27.26,27.38]},{"s":1,"a":28.06,"b":31.62,"text":"Contrast means text must stand out clearly from its background.","w":[28.12,28.78,29.12,29.68,29.9,30.22,30.44,30.86,31,31.14]},{"s":1,"a":31.92,"b":36.79,"text":"Dark text on a light background is easy to read. Pale grey on white is not.","w":[31.94,32.28,32.68,32.8,32.88,33.12,33.68,33.88,34.12,34.24,35.04,35.36,35.76,35.92,36.38,36.54]},{"s":1,"a":37.09,"b":39.88,"text":"Alignment means lining things up along shared edges.","w":[37.14,37.66,38,38.38,38.7,38.84,39.18,39.5]},{"s":1,"a":40.18,"b":43.13,"text":"When edges line up, the screen feels ordered and calm.","w":[40.22,40.48,40.78,41.08,41.56,41.68,42.02,42.38,42.66,42.78]},{"s":2,"a":43.98,"b":47.74,"text":"Proximity means things that belong together sit close together.","w":[44,44.66,45.04,45.32,45.48,45.8,46.62,46.9,47.26]},{"s":2,"a":48.04,"b":51.89,"text":"Use more space between groups, so each group reads as one unit.","w":[48.2,48.38,48.58,48.94,49.32,50.04,50.32,50.52,50.86,51.14,51.38,51.6]},{"s":2,"a":52.19,"b":55.21,"text":"White space is empty space, and it is not wasted.","w":[52.26,52.52,52.9,53.1,53.38,54.16,54.28,54.4,54.56,54.8]},{"s":2,"a":55.51,"b":59.15,"text":"It lets the eye rest and shows where groups begin and end.","w":[55.58,55.7,55.94,56.2,56.4,57.12,57.3,57.64,57.84,58.2,58.66,58.88]},{"s":2,"a":59.45,"b":65.32,"text":"Consistency means the same kind of thing looks and behaves the same everywhere. Main buttons share one style.","w":[59.46,60.22,60.48,60.64,60.96,61.18,61.28,61.52,61.82,61.92,62.3,62.44,62.74,63.78,64.08,64.48,64.8,64.96]},{"s":2,"a":65.62,"b":71.93,"text":"Keep to a small set: one or two typefaces, a few sizes, and one main colour for the main action.","w":[65.64,65.9,66.08,66.18,66.54,67.42,67.56,67.7,67.9,68.76,68.86,69.1,70,70.26,70.46,70.72,71.04,71.18,71.3,71.58]},{"s":2,"a":72.23,"b":76.12,"text":"Use neutral colours for the rest, and one primary button per screen.","w":[72.34,72.58,72.92,73.28,73.4,73.52,74.3,74.54,74.76,75.26,75.56,75.74]},{"s":3,"a":76.97,"b":84.17,"text":"Picture a crowded sign up screen with five colours, a mix of centred and left aligned text, and three equally loud buttons.","w":[76.98,77.38,77.5,77.92,78.2,78.3,78.68,78.9,79.22,80.06,80.16,80.42,80.58,81.16,81.32,81.56,81.88,82.46,82.64,83.04,83.42,83.7]},{"s":3,"a":84.47,"b":85.56,"text":"Fix it step by step.","w":[84.52,84.8,84.94,85.22,85.4]},{"s":3,"a":85.86,"b":88.88,"text":"Use one clear heading, so the purpose is noticed first.","w":[85.96,86.24,86.42,86.68,87.34,87.48,87.64,88.02,88.16,88.48]},{"s":3,"a":89.18,"b":92.94,"text":"Left align the labels, so the eye moves down a clean edge.","w":[89.24,89.58,89.86,89.98,90.82,90.96,91.26,91.44,91.82,92.16,92.26,92.66]},{"s":3,"a":93.24,"b":97.28,"text":"Place each label close to its field, so they read as one pair.","w":[93.3,93.88,94.16,94.52,94.8,94.94,95.1,95.88,96.04,96.26,96.54,96.78,96.94]},{"s":3,"a":97.58,"b":101.03,"text":"Add more space between groups, so the form feels ordered.","w":[97.66,97.84,98.08,98.4,98.76,99.78,99.92,100.06,100.36,100.72]},{"s":3,"a":101.33,"b":105.73,"text":"Keep one main button for signing up, and make the other choices a quiet text link.","w":[101.38,101.74,101.9,102.14,102.44,102.6,102.96,103.52,103.64,103.84,104,104.2,104.66,104.78,105.12,105.44]},{"s":4,"a":106.58,"b":111.89,"text":"Quick check. A screen has two buttons, Save and Cancel, and they look identical.","w":[106.6,106.82,107.64,107.72,108.08,108.3,108.5,109.44,109.96,110.1,110.84,110.94,111.08,111.32]},{"s":4,"a":112.19,"b":113.67,"text":"What should change, and why?","w":[112.26,112.44,112.64,113.26,113.4]},{"s":4,"a":114.12,"b":116.36,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[114.14,114.48,114.74,114.88,115.18,115.82,116.02]},{"s":5,"a":117.21,"b":121.06,"text":"Make Save stand out as the main action, and make Cancel quieter.","w":[117.3,117.58,117.9,118.28,118.5,118.62,118.74,119.02,119.78,119.92,120.2,120.62]},{"s":5,"a":121.36,"b":125.48,"text":"That shows the hierarchy, so the user sees what to do next.","w":[121.42,121.74,122.1,122.24,123.38,123.56,123.78,124.14,124.48,124.7,124.84,125.02]},{"s":6,"a":126.33,"b":133.7,"text":"Common mistake one. Making everything bold, so nothing stands out. Use bold only for the most important thing.","w":[126.38,126.74,127.28,127.94,128.36,128.76,129.52,129.76,130.1,130.48,131.4,131.66,132.22,132.5,132.64,132.78,133.02,133.44]},{"s":6,"a":134,"b":140.05,"text":"Common mistake two. Too many colours and fonts. Choose one or two typefaces and a small colour set.","w":[134.04,134.38,134.76,135.54,135.76,136.02,136.42,136.56,137.5,137.94,138.08,138.18,138.4,139.02,139.14,139.24,139.54,139.84]},{"s":6,"a":140.35,"b":148.19,"text":"Common mistake three. Low contrast grey text and uneven spacing. Use strong contrast and align and space items consistently.","w":[140.38,140.72,141.12,141.86,142.12,142.72,143,143.38,143.6,144.02,145.06,145.22,145.56,146.12,146.26,146.68,146.84,147.22,147.5]},{"s":7,"a":149.04,"b":152.4,"text":"Recap. Use hierarchy to show what matters first.","w":[149.1,150.18,150.38,150.98,151.16,151.38,151.56,151.96]},{"s":7,"a":152.7,"b":157.14,"text":"Use contrast, alignment, proximity and white space to make the screen clear.","w":[152.8,153,153.82,154.52,155.22,155.38,155.64,156.02,156.12,156.3,156.4,156.76]},{"s":7,"a":157.44,"b":162.51,"text":"Use consistency and a small set of styles, with one primary button per screen.","w":[157.56,157.76,158.66,158.78,158.94,159.34,159.54,159.66,160.5,160.82,161.02,161.52,161.84,162.08]},{"s":7,"a":162.81,"b":168.15,"text":"Top tip: if everything shouts, nothing is heard, so make one thing clearly main.","w":[162.82,163.14,163.8,164.04,164.44,165.24,165.6,165.72,166.4,166.6,166.94,167.14,167.44,167.86]},{"s":7,"a":168.45,"b":172.06,"text":"Keep practising with simple screens, and Knowzone will help you grow.","w":[168.5,168.72,169.22,169.38,169.66,170.62,170.78,171.28,171.46,171.64,171.76]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"The puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Ever missed a button you needed?"},{"at":3.64,"kind":"term","text":"Visual design basics","detail":"The screen shows what matters first"},{"at":10,"kind":"text","text":"A simple skill you can learn"}]},{"at":12.5,"heading":"Visual hierarchy","items":[{"at":12.65,"kind":"term","text":"Visual hierarchy","detail":"The most important thing is noticed first"},{"at":16.31,"kind":"text","text":"Size, weight, colour, contrast, position"},{"at":20.18,"kind":"term","text":"Weight","detail":"Bold text pulls the eye"}]},{"at":23.35,"heading":"Contrast & alignment","items":[{"at":23.5,"kind":"text","text":"Scan from the top; in left-to-right languages, from left"},{"at":27.96,"kind":"term","text":"Contrast","detail":"Text must stand out from its background"},{"at":31.82,"kind":"text","text":"Dark on light easy; pale grey on white not"},{"at":36.99,"kind":"term","text":"Alignment","detail":"Line things up along shared edges"},{"at":40.08,"kind":"text","text":"Aligned edges feel ordered and calm"}]},{"at":43.73,"heading":"Proximity & white space","items":[{"at":43.88,"kind":"term","text":"Proximity","detail":"Things that belong together sit close"},{"at":47.94,"kind":"text","text":"More space between groups"},{"at":52.09,"kind":"term","text":"White space","detail":"Empty space is not wasted"},{"at":55.41,"kind":"text","text":"Lets the eye rest; shows group edges"}]},{"at":59.2,"heading":"Consistency","items":[{"at":59.35,"kind":"term","text":"Consistency","detail":"Same kind of thing looks and behaves the same"},{"at":65.52,"kind":"text","text":"1–2 typefaces, few sizes, one main colour"},{"at":72.13,"kind":"text","text":"Neutral colours; one primary button per screen"}]},{"at":76.72,"heading":"Fix a sign-up screen","items":[{"at":76.87,"kind":"text","text":"Crowded: 5 colours, mixed alignment, 3 loud buttons"},{"at":84.37,"kind":"text","text":"Fix it step by step"}]},{"at":85.61,"heading":"Step-by-step fixes","items":[{"at":85.76,"kind":"text","text":"One clear heading → purpose noticed first"},{"at":89.08,"kind":"text","text":"Left-align labels → clean edge"},{"at":93.14,"kind":"text","text":"Label close to field → one pair"},{"at":97.48,"kind":"text","text":"More space between groups → ordered"},{"at":101.23,"kind":"text","text":"One main sign-up button; others quiet links"}]},{"at":106.16,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":106.16,"kind":"question","text":"A screen has two buttons, Save and Cancel, and they look identical. What should change, and why?"}]},{"at":116.96,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":117.11,"kind":"text","text":"Save = main action; Cancel = quieter"},{"at":121.26,"kind":"text","text":"Hierarchy shows what to do next"}]},{"at":126.08,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":126.23,"kind":"wrong","text":"Everything bold"},{"at":133.9,"kind":"wrong","text":"Too many colours and fonts"},{"at":140.25,"kind":"wrong","text":"Low contrast; uneven spacing"}]},{"at":148.79,"heading":"Recap & top tip","items":[{"at":148.94,"kind":"text","text":"Hierarchy shows what matters first"},{"at":152.6,"kind":"text","text":"Contrast, alignment, proximity, white space"},{"at":157.34,"kind":"text","text":"Consistency; small style set; one primary button"},{"at":162.71,"kind":"tip","text":"If everything shouts, nothing is heard: make one thing main"},{"at":168.35,"kind":"text","text":"Practise simple screens; Knowzone helps you grow"}]}],"check":{"at":116.61,"seconds":10,"question":"A screen has two buttons, Save and Cancel, and they look identical. What should change, and why?","answer":"Make Save stand out as the main action; make Cancel quieter. This shows hierarchy so the user sees what to do next."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}